<title>RUSSIA: Russian 1996 trade surplus widens to $28.8 billion.</title>
<headline>Russian 1996 trade surplus widens to $28.8 billion.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia posted a trade surplus of $28.8 billion in 1996 according to preliminary data after a $21.6 billion surplus in 1995, the State Statistics Committee said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Excluding trade with other members of CIS:</p>
<p>RUSSIAN MERCHANDISE TRADE Jan-Dec 96  Jan-Nov 96  Jan-Dec 95</p>
<p>    exports			    71.0	  64.6	  n/a</p>
<p>    imports			    42.2	  38.7	  n/a</p>
<p>    trade balance		   +28.8	 +25.9	+21.6</p>
<p>Total trade, including other members of CIS</p>
<p>RUSSIAN MERCHANDISE TRADE Jan-Dec 96  Jan-Nov 96  Jan-Dec 95</p>
<p>    exports			    87.7	  80.2	  n/a</p>
<p>    imports			    59.7	  55.0	  n/a</p>
<p>    trade balance		   +28.0	 +25.2	+20.2</p>
<p>Notes -- Figures in billion dollars, FOB.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
